(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/id "adr-2609111900-predicting-what-a-repair-must-not-change-is-what-made-it-readable")
  (:adr/topic "q9-credrow-backfill")
  (:adr/title "Predicting what a repair must NOT change is what made eleven regenerations readable")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Opus 5"))
  (:adr/repos (vector "com-junkawasaki/root" "kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang"))
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609111800-twenty-of-twenty-have-a-harness-and-eleven-carry-a-defect-it-cannot-see"))
  (:adr/body
  "## What was repaired

Eleven of the twenty wave-1 pilots shipped a `cred-row` that emitted its ref
field TWICE -- a duplicate JSON key -- next to a `quantity` field the repository
does not declare. Each names a different field, which is what makes it
recognisable rather than a copy-paste:

    com-8th-wall sceneId    com-abb-800xa tagId       com-accelbyte playerId
    com-ach-network customerId               com-acorrd-standards policyId
    com-acquia assetId      com-adobe projectId       com-ads-b-aviation objectId
    com-agleader fieldId    com-agones playerId       com-airbyte connectorId

All eleven regenerated with the current generator. A re-scan of the cohort now
reports zero.

## Nothing that was checking could see it

`amu check` returns `:ok true`: the object is built with `jkv` calls and the
compiler has no schema for its contents. And no layer of the parity harness
reads `cred-row` -- route count, as-int, as-bool, page-limit and the entity
table all derive from `entity-specs` or from a fixed table of strings.

So this was not caught by a check. It was caught by asking, after building the
harness, what the harness still could not see.

## The prediction, made before the runs

A regeneration that rewrites `cred-row` and nothing else must leave every
harness layer exactly where it was, because no layer reads `cred-row`. That was
written down first and then measured on all eleven:

    compared 23 or 29 rows per repository
    differ    exactly 1, and always the as-int \"12abc\" control

If a second row had moved, the correct conclusion would not have been \"the
repair worked\" -- it would have been that the regeneration changed something
else as well, and the change would have needed finding before landing.

This is the same instrument as `oracle-float-divergence` during the
com-abb-robotics regeneration: a value that MUST NOT move is what lets a page of
values that did move be read. The difference here is that the prediction covered
every layer rather than one oracle, so the eleven runs are eleven confirmations
rather than eleven repetitions.

## Verification

Each of the eleven: regenerated, `amu check :ok true`, compiled to
aarch64-macos, executed through `tools/kexe_loader.c`, and every harness layer
re-compared afterwards.

## What is left

The harnesses themselves are now uneven. Nine were generated before the
entity-table layer existed and compare 23 rows; eleven compare 29. That shows up
directly in the numbers above and is the next thing to level.

Nothing in this iteration touched the fixture-shaped layers -- store, filter,
pagination, handler, expand -- which remain present only in the four
hand-written harnesses.")))
